    "summary": "Asafo flag with a central chequerboard pattern (there are no figurative elements) of white and blue squares of silk; this is edged on three sides by rectangles of white cotton and red and blue silk which terminate in a fringe of cut white cotton. The fourth side has a wide band of white cotton with ties. In the upper corner, where a Union Jack is often placed, is a pattern of red, blue and white triangles which may signify the Dutch flag.",
